.TH CPROVER "1" "March 1, 2026" "cprover-6.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cprover \- verify C programs using state\-based encoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cprover
.RI [ options ]
.I source\-file.c
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cprover
is an experimental verification tool for C programs.
It reads a C source file, constructs a GOTO program (the intermediate
representation used by the CProver tool suite), and encodes the program
into a set of logical constraints over program states.
The built\-in solver then attempts to prove that all assertions in the
program hold, using an iterative approach based on inductiveness
checking and generalization.
.PP
Unlike
.BR cbmc (1),
which performs bounded model checking by unwinding loops to a fixed
depth,
.B cprover
uses a state\-based encoding that models the program heap with custom
operators for memory allocation, deallocation, and pointer
dereferencing.
The solver iteratively checks whether candidate invariants are
inductive and generalizes them when they are too weak.
.PP
By default,
.B cprover
instruments the program with safety checks (array bounds, pointer
validity) and then runs the built\-in solver.
The formula can also be exported in SMT\-LIB2 or text format for
inspection or use with external tools.
.PP
When
.B \-\-contract
is given,
.B cprover
checks the specified function against its contract (requires
.B __CPROVER_requires
and
.B __CPROVER_ensures
annotations in the source).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Verification"
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-safety\fR
Disable the automatic safety checks (pointer safety, array bounds).
Only user\-specified assertions will be checked.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-assertions\fR
Remove all assertions from the program.
This is useful when only the encoding output is desired.
.TP
\fB\-\-contract\fR \fIfunction\fR
Check the contract of the given \fIfunction\fR.
The function must have
.B __CPROVER_requires
and
.B __CPROVER_ensures
annotations.
.TP
\fB\-\-unwind\fR \fIN\fR
Set the loop unwinding limit to \fIN\fR (default is 1).
.TP
\fB\-\-trace\fR
Print a counterexample trace when a property is refuted.
.TP
\fB\-\-solve\fR
Run the built\-in solver even when formula output
(\fB\-\-smt2\fR or \fB\-\-text\fR) is requested.
By default, formula output suppresses solving.
.SS "Formula Output"
.TP
\fB\-\-smt2\fR
Output the state encoding as an SMT\-LIB2 formula.
When this option is given, function call inlining is performed by
default (use \fB\-\-no\-inline\fR to suppress).
.TP
\fB\-\-text\fR
Output the state encoding in a human\-readable text format.
.TP
\fB\-\-outfile\fR \fIfile\fR
Write the formula to \fIfile\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
\fB\-\-variables\fR
Use variable\-based encoding instead of state\-based encoding.
Implies inlining.
.SS "Program Transformations"
.TP
\fB\-\-inline\fR
Perform function call inlining before generating the formula.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-inline\fR
Suppress the automatic inlining that \fB\-\-smt2\fR enables by default.
.SS "Diagnostics"
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-goto\-functions\fR
Print the GOTO intermediate representation and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-loops\fR
Print loop identifiers and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-functions\-with\-loops\fR
Print the names of functions that contain loops and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-properties\fR
Print the properties (assertions) found in the program and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-goto\-model\fR
Run internal consistency checks on the GOTO model.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output, including solver progress and iteration
details.
.SS "Preprocessor"
.TP
\fB\-D\fR \fIname\fR[=\fIvalue\fR]
Define a preprocessor macro.
.TP
\fB\-I\fR \fIpath\fR
Add \fIpath\fR to the preprocessor include search path.
.TP
\fB\-\-32\fR
Set the architecture to 32\-bit mode.
.TP
\fB\-\-64\fR
Set the architecture to 64\-bit mode.
.SS "General"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-?\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version number and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All properties verified successfully (or \fB\-\-help\fR/\fB\-\-version\fR
was given).
.TP
.B 1
Usage error (invalid command line).
.TP
.B 2
Parse error (source file could not be processed).
.TP
.B 6
Internal error, incorrect task, or unexpected exception.
.TP
.B 10
At least one property was refuted (verification unsafe).
.SH EXAMPLES
Verify a C source file with default safety checks:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
cprover main.c
.EE
.in
.PP
Export the state encoding as an SMT\-LIB2 formula:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
cprover \-\-smt2 \-\-outfile formula.smt2 main.c
.EE
.in
.PP
Check a function contract with a counterexample trace:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
cprover \-\-contract my_function \-\-trace main.c
.EE
.in
.SH ENVIRONMENT
All tools honor the TMPDIR environment variable when generating
temporary files and directories.
.SH BUGS
.B cprover
is experimental.
The built\-in solver uses custom operators for heap modeling that are
not supported by standard SMT solvers, so the SMT\-LIB2 output is
primarily useful for inspection rather than for feeding into external
solvers.
.PP
If you encounter a problem please create an issue at
.B https://github.com/diffblue/cbmc/issues
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cbmc (1),
.BR goto\-cc (1),
